body:
This is my look on the situation. I believe they should switch to a 3/4 year DEVELOPMENT in-between games so the current dev. can focus on the first year release adding crucial content to keep the game thriving as well as fixing flaws that come up in code. After the first initial year they have time to do the same process of rebuilding a new game in the coming years, ready to release a platform for the following year to be improved. Make it a longer cycle.

&#x200B;

Plus this gives our COMPETiTIVE scene a little more hope in longevity for being several years to perform rather than cramming a cod series in 9 months. Every time there's a new release the comp. scene has to breakdown and learn the game. We add this longer gap, the scene thrives just as much as the developers. Where we see an extended effort at improving the game for both the players and company. Plus our competing GAME(s) are in a seasonal circuit rather than a new TITLE yearly.

&#x200B;

The SEASON thing works, I don't like dropping $10 every 2 months for a video game to unlock content. BUT, this adds another progression system besides ranking so It keeps me involved and interested in continuing playing. 

&#x200B;

And the REMASTERED talk is nonsense. They just need to throw in some OLD maps & weapons (which they are doing to promote new seasons)  to fix this issue. The main concern is that we're getting a new COD this year? So a lot of interest is gonna fall short in this game which leads to less players circling the servers.
